{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"jq -r '.references[] | [.citation_key,.title,.query] | @tsv' references_provenance.json; printf '\\\\n--- GAP LOCATION ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'section\\\\{Related Work|Calibration and adaptation|our study instead evaluates joint' paper.tex; printf '\\\\n--- MEMORY FILES ---\\\\n'; ls -l global_memory/memory.md global_memory/memory.jsonl .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\"","aggregated_output":"Vovk2005\tAlgorithmic Learning in a Random World\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1007/b106715\nPapadopoulos2002\tInductive Confidence Machines for Regression\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1007/3-540-36755-1_29\nLei2018\tDistribution-Free Predictive Inference for Regression\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1080/01621459.2017.1307116\nBarber2021Jackknife\tPredictive inference with the jackknife+\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1214/20-AOS1965\nTibshirani2019\tConformal Prediction Under Covariate Shift\tDirect identifier lookup: arxiv:1904.06019\nAngelopoulos2021\tA Gentle Introduction to Conformal Prediction and Distribution-Free Uncertainty Quantification\tDirect identifier lookup: arxiv:2107.07511\nAitchison1982\tThe Statistical Analysis of Compositional Data\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1111/j.2517-6161.1982.tb01195.x\nEgozcue2003\tIsometric Logratio Transformations for Compositional Data Analysis\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1023/A:1023818214614\nAitchisonShen1980\tLogistic-normal distributions:Some properties and uses\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1093/biomet/67.2.261\nPawlowsky2011\tCompositional Data Analysis\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1002/9781119976462\nSchaferStrimmer2005\tA Shrinkage Approach to Large-Scale Covariance Matrix Estimation and Implications for Functional Genomics\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.2202/1544-6115.1175\nChen2010\tShrinkage Algorithms for MMSE Covariance Estimation\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1109/TSP.2010.2053029\nHoerlKennard1970\tRidge Regression: Biased Estimation for Nonorthogonal Problems\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1080/00401706.1970.10488634\nStone1974\tCross-Validatory Choice and Assessment of Statistical Predictions\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1111/j.2517-6161.1974.tb00994.x\nGeisser1975\tThe Predictive Sample Reuse Method with Applications\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1080/01621459.1975.10479865\nBrown2001\tInterval Estimation for a Binomial Proportion\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1214/ss/1009213286\nEfron1979\tBootstrap Methods: Another Look at the Jackknife\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1214/aos/1176344552\nDavison1997\tBootstrap Methods and their Application\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1017/CBO9780511802843\nRomano2019\tConformalized Quantile Regression\tDirect identifier lookup: arxiv:1905.03222\nBarber2021Limits\tThe limits of distribution-free conditional predictive inference\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1093/imaiai/iaaa017\nBarber2023\tConformal prediction beyond exchangeability\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1214/23-AOS2276\nGneiting2007\tStrictly Proper Scoring Rules, Prediction, and Estimation\tDirect identifier lookup: 10.1198/016214506000001437\nVovk2012\tConditional validity of inductive conformal predictors\tDirect identifier lookup: arxiv:1209.2673\nRomano2020\tClassification with Valid and Adaptive Coverage\tDirect identifier lookup: arxiv:2006.02544\nDing2023\tClass-Conditional Conformal Prediction with Many Classes\tDirect identifier lookup: arxiv:2306.09335\n\n--- GAP LOCATION ---\n53:\\section{Related Work}\n57:\\paragraph{Calibration and adaptation.}\n58:Split-conformal regression allows a flexible fitted score while retaining marginal calibration \\citep{Lei2018}. Conformalized quantile regression adapts interval width to heteroskedasticity \\citep{Romano2019}; our study instead evaluates joint multivariate membership after residual rescaling. Cross-validation and predictive sample reuse motivate held-out residual estimation \\citep{Stone1974,Geisser1975}, but training residual cross-fitting is not itself a conformal procedure. In particular, the present construction is not jackknife+: that method combines leave-one-out predictions and residuals in its region construction \\citep{Barber2021Jackknife}. Our separate calibration sample remains essential.\n\n--- MEMORY FILES ---\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 agent agent 14321 Nov  2 14:28 .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 22303 Nov  7 06:48 global_memory/memory.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 23236 Nov  7 06:48 global_memory/memory.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
